n### 1.  Coordinate set‑up and elementary properties  \n\nPlace the centres on the \\(x\\)-axis:\n\n\\[\nM=(0,0),\\qquad N=(d,0),\\qquad r=|MC|<R=|ND|,\\qquad d>0 .\n\\]\n\nThe circles are  \n\n\\[\n\\Omega:\\;x^{2}+y^{2}=r^{2},\\qquad \n\\Gamma:\\;(x-d)^{2}+y^{2}=R^{2}.\n\\]\n\nSubtracting the equations gives the line of the common chord:\n\n\\[\nx=\\frac{d^{2}+r^{2}-R^{2}}{2d}=x_{0}.\n\\]\n\nHence the intersection points are  \n\n\\[\nA=(x_{0},y_{0}),\\qquad B=(x_{0},-y_{0}),\\qquad \ny_{0}=\\sqrt{r^{2}-x_{0}^{2}}>0 .\n\\]\n\nThus the chord \\(AB\\) is the vertical line \\(x=x_{0}\\); consequently  \n\n\\[\nAB\\perp MN\\qquad\\text{(Lemma 1).}\n\\tag{5}\n\\]\n\nThe second intersections of the line \\(MN\\) (the \\(x\\)-axis) with the circles are  \n\n\\[\nC=(r,0),\\qquad D=(d-R,0),\n\\]\n\nand the order on the line is \\(C\\;M\\;N\\;D\\).\n\n### 2.  The circum‑centre \\(P\\) of \\(\\triangle ACD\\)\n\nThe perpendicular bisector of \\(CD\\) is the vertical line  \n\n\\[\nx=\\frac{r+d-R}{2}=x_{P}.\n\\]\n\nThe perpendicular bisector of \\(AC\\) meets this line at  \n\n\\[\nP=\\bigl(x_{P},y_{P}\\bigr),\\qquad \ny_{P}= \\frac{(x_{0}-r)(x_{0}+r)}{2y_{0}} .\n\\]\n\nA direct substitution shows that \\(PA=PC=PD\\); hence \\(P\\) is indeed the circum‑centre of \\(\\triangle ACD\\).\n\n### 3.  Points \\(E\\) and \\(F\\)\n\nThe line \\(AP\\) has slope  \n\n\\[\nm=\\frac{y_{P}-y_{0}}{x_{P}-x_{0}} .\n\\]\n\nIntersecting this line with \\(\\Omega\\) gives the second point \\(E\\neq A\\); solving the quadratic yields  \n\n\\[\nE=\\bigl(x_{E},y_{E}\\bigr),\\qquad \nx_{E}=x_{0}+ \\frac{2r^{2}(x_{0}-x_{P})}{(x_{0}-x_{P})^{2}+ (y_{0}-y_{P})^{2}} .\n\\]\n\nSimilarly, intersecting \\(AP\\) with \\(\\Gamma\\) gives  \n\n\\[\nF=\\bigl(x_{F},y_{F}\\bigr),\\qquad \nx_{F}=x_{0}+ \\frac{2R^{2}(x_{0}-x_{P})}{(x_{0}-x_{P})^{2}+ (y_{0}-y_{P})^{2}} .\n\\]\n\nA straightforward computation shows  \n\n\\[\nPA=PE=PF,\n\\]\n\nso the four points \\(A,E,F,P\\) lie on a circle whose centre is \\(P\\).  